#### [Example 2 - Testing the `ToString` method](https://microsoft.github.io/Pex/gallery/PEX_Gallery_Code/Framework/CustomFramework/1.0.1482.0/ToStringContract/ToStringContract.cs) 

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text;

using Microsoft.Pex.Framework;
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Settings;
using Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Exceptions;

using NUnit.Framework;

namespace CustomFramework
{
  [TestFixture, PexClass] 
  public partial class ToStringContract
  {
    // Assume an object type to be tested
    public class MyObject 
    {
      public int Id { get; set;}
      public string Name { get; set; }
      public override string ToString() 
      {
          return this.Id + " " + this.Name;
      }
    } 

    [PexMethod]
    public void Test(MyObject obj)
    {
      // Assume that the object is not null
      AssumePrecondition.IsNotNull(obj);

      // Observe the returned string
      PexObserve.ValueForViewing("obj.ToString", obj.ToString());
    }
  }
}
```

## Further Reading

For further reading on Pex, there are several articles on Microsoft's official website:

1. [Unit Testing and Code Coverage with Pex](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/dn903472.aspx)
2. [Visual Studio 2015 Update 2 Preview: Code Coverage for Unit Tests](https://blogs.msdn.microsoft.com/devops/2015/07/15/visual-studio-2015-update-2-preview-code-coverage-for-unit-tests/)
3. [Using Microsoft.Pex for Unit Testing](https://blogs.msdn.microsoft.com/devops/2012/02/04/using-microsoft-pex-for-unit-testing/)
4. [Unit Testing with Microsoft.Pex](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/dn267185.aspx)

Remember to follow your team's software testing policies. If a unit testing tool isn't being used, or isn't being used properly, it may introduce some false positives and negatives, and potentially affect testing results. Keep your team's attention on true test coverage in addition to any tools provided. 
Also note that, certain tests might not be valid or relevant for certain conditions so it's good to remember that good testing also includes considering these special cases according to your project's conditions.

Happy testing.

